It is Thursday evening, half past five.
I am at the badminton club.
I have swapped my work clothes for sports clothes.
I go to the reception and rent a racket.
Timo is already waiting on the court.
We are playing doubles today.
Between the rallies we take a short break.
Timo asks me about my work.
"How is it going at the office, Maya?" he asks.
I tell him about the new project.
"It is great," I answer.
"I have been a software engineer for many years."
"But I am properly working together with the whole team for the first time."
Timo smiles and takes his racket.
"That sounds super!"
"You have settled in well," he says.
We keep playing, and I am very proud.
I have really arrived professionally in Berlin.
